  "id": "Compound::DB00717 - Gene::6462",
  "verbalization": "Norethindrone, a progestin, is linked to Shbg through a shared pathway involving 17Beta-Hydroxy Steroid and Progestin. The evidence suggests that Norethindrone, as part of the Progesterone Congeners group, binds to Shbg via Etonogestrel, which is a member of this group. This relationship is supported by the lowest common ancestor (LCA) of Norethindrone and Etonogestrel, which is 17Beta-Hydroxy Steroid and Progestin. The mechanism appears to involve a common pathway where Norethindrone and Etonogestrel both interact with Shbg through a shared biological process. The evidence from both paths indicates that Norethindrone may influence Shbg through Etonogestrel, suggesting a potential role in the regulation of Shbg through progestin-related pathways. The integration of these findings highlights a possible dependency on progestin-like compounds to modulate Shbg, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
